## Before handing the bundle back

1. Confirm `content/pages.json` and `editingContract.pageOrder` contain the same pages in the same order.
2. Confirm every page exists at the bundle root and has a matching `editingContract.pageDataIds` entry.
3. Confirm each page has exactly one `#content` root and its matching `section[data-section-id]`.
4. Search the whole book for duplicate or missing `data-id` values.
5. Confirm every `activities` and `nonActivities` entry matches `pageOrder`, with no duplicate or conflicting classifications.
6. Confirm page images resolve from `images/`.
7. Confirm no custom or remote stylesheets and no custom external scripts were added.
8. Zip the contents of this directory without introducing another internal layout.

ADT Studio performs the same checks during import and will explain any incompatibility instead of trying to guess how a custom structure should map back into the pipeline.
